r loans for all students and  a very  generous loan forgiveness program after  graduation  for students going into the social  sector at any point in their career  so we hope that today's session has been  helpful in answering some of your big  questions about applying to stanford gsb  to continue on we encourage you to check  out mystanford.nbc  you can take a short quiz to personalize  your dashboard  you can keep track of your application  progress and events  and find out about other find out  other information about stanford  tailored to your interests  so next my colleague allison and i are  going to take your questions which you  can submit in the q a box  jessica there's one question here that i  think we should answer from  jimmy who wants to understand the  process of how to apply for the fee  waiver  yes that's a great question so the fee  waiver will be  automatically applied if you are a  citizen of  a latin american country or a country in  the regions that i named earlier  and your salary converts to  40 000 or less  in u.s currency so that's that happens  automatically if you  um if you feel that the  fee waiver should apply to you but it's  not happening automatically  feel free to reach out to to our office  we want to make sure that  you're able to access that program so  susanna asks does  the minimum gmat score depend on the  industry  and so i'll preface this by saying  there's no minimum  gmat score you can take a look at our  class profile on our website if you want  to get a sense of  where most of our students fall in terms  of their scores but  there's no minimum score and as i  mentioned this is a holistic  process so for as much attention as  scores get  ultimately we're really interested in  the whole person  part of that is determining whether or  not you  have the academic preparation to  [Music]  succeed in our classes but again  it's a holistic process we're interested  in your  academic aptitude and your academic  attitude  and we 